<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Order of Assassins</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Assassin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Order of Assassins is the popular name for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismaili-state">Nizari Ismailis</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a>, founded under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-i-sabbah">Hasan-i Sabbah</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a> mountains. Arising from the Fatimid succession crisis of 1094, they were known for targeted killings of political opponents. Their name gave rise to the English word assassin, and their lineage continues through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aga-khan">Aga Khan</a>, a lasting legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins.jpg" alt="Order of Assassins" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Basawan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Assassins2-alamut.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
